{"id":"mahabharata-5-188","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":188,"title":"अष्टाशीत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 188 · Amba enters the fire","summary":{"en":"Shiva appears to Amba and grants her boon: she will be born again as a woman, become a man, and be the cause of Bhishma's death. Amba builds a pyre and enters the fire, declaring that it is for the death of Bhishma.","kn":"ಶಿವನು ಅಂಬೆಗೆ ಪ್ರತ್ಯಕ್ಷನಾಗಿ ವರ ನೀಡುತ್ತಾನೆ: ಅವಳು ಮತ್ತೆ ಸ್ತ್ರೀಯಾಗಿ ಹುಟ್ಟಿ ಪುರುಷಳಾಗಿ ಭೀಷ್ಮನ ಮರಣಕ್ಕೆ ಕಾರಣಳಾಗುವಳು. ಅಂಬೆ ಚಿತೆ ನಿರ್ಮಿಸಿ ಭೀಷ್ಮವಧೆಗಾಗಿ ಎಂದು ಘೋಷಿಸಿ ಅಗ್ನಿಪ್ರವೇಶ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"शिव अम्बा के सामने प्रकट होकर वर देते हैं: वह फिर स्त्री के रूप में जन्म लेगी, पुरुष बनेगी और भीष्म की मृत्यु का कारण बनेगी। अम्बा चिता बनाकर यह घोषणा करती हुई अग्नि में प्रवेश करती है कि यह भीष्म के वध के लिए है।","te":"శివుడు అంబకు ప్రత్యక్షమై వరమిస్తాడు: ఆమె మళ్లీ స్త్రీగా పుట్టి పురుషునిగా మారి భీష్ముని మరణానికి కారణమవుతుంది. అంబ చితిని నిర్మించి భీష్మవధ కోసమని ప్రకటిస్తూ అగ్నిప్రవేశం చేస్తుంది.","ta":"ஶிவன் அம்பைக்குத் தோன்றி வரம் அளிக்கிறார்: அவள் மீண்டும் பெண்ணாகப் பிறந்து ஆணாக மாறிப் பீஷ்மரின் சாவுக்குக் காரணமாவாள். அம்பை சிதை அமைத்துப் பீஷ்மரைக் கொல்லவே என்று அறிவித்துத் தீயில் புகுகிறாள்.","ml":"ശിവൻ അംബയ്ക്ക് പ്രത്യക്ഷനായി വരം നൽകുന്നു: അവൾ വീണ്ടും സ്ത്രീയായി ജനിക്കും, പുരുഷനായി മാറും, ഭീഷ്മരുടെ മരണത്തിന് കാരണമാകും. അംബ ചിത കൂട്ടി അഗ്നിയിൽ പ്രവേശിക്കുന്നു; ഭീഷ്മരുടെ മരണത്തിനാണിതെന്ന് അവൾ പ്രഖ്യാപിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.188; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"अम्बोपाख्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Ambopakhyana Parva (The story of Amba)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततस्ते तापसाः सर्वे तपसे धृतनिश्चयाम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा न्यवर्तयंस्तात किं कार्यमिति चाब्रुवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the ascetics, seeing her firmly set on austerity, tried to turn her back, my dear, and asked what they could do for her."}},{"n":2,"text":"तानुवाच ततः कन्या तपोवृद्धानृषींस्तदा ।\nनिराकृतास्मि भीष्मेण भ्रंशिता पतिधर्मतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The maiden then said to those sages, grown great in austerity: \"I have been spurned by Bhishma and cast out from the duty of a wife to a husband.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"वधार्थं तस्य दीक्षा मे न लोकार्थं तपोधनाः ।\nनिहत्य भीष्मं गच्छेयं शान्तिमित्येव निश्चयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"My vow is for killing him, not for gaining any world, O ascetics. My resolve is to go to peace only after I have killed Bhishma.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"यत्कृते दुःखवसतिमिमां प्राप्तास्मि शाश्वतीम् ।\nपतिलोकाद्विहीना च नैव स्त्री न पुमानिह ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Because of him I have fallen into this lasting life of misery, cut off from a husband's world, neither woman nor man here.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"नाहत्वा युधि गाङ्गेयं निवर्तेयं तपोधनाः ।\nएष मे हृदि संकल्पो यदर्थमिदमुद्यतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I will not turn back, ascetics, without killing the son of Ganga in battle. This is the resolve in my heart for which I have taken this up.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"स्त्रीभावे परिनिर्विण्णा पुंस्त्वार्थे कृतनिश्चया ।\nभीष्मे प्रतिचिकीर्षामि नास्मि वार्येति वै पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Weary of being a woman and set on becoming a man, I mean to take vengeance on Bhishma. Do not hold me back again.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"तां देवो दर्शयामास शूलपाणिरुमापतिः ।\nमध्ये तेषां महर्षीणां स्वेन रूपेण भामिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the god Shiva, bearer of the trident and husband of Uma, showed himself in his own form to the lady among those great sages."}},{"n":8,"text":"छन्द्यमाना वरेणाथ सा वव्रे मत्पराजयम् ।\nवधिष्यसीति तां देवः प्रत्युवाच मनस्विनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Offered a boon, she chose my defeat, and the god answered that spirited woman: \"You will kill him.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"ततः सा पुनरेवाथ कन्या रुद्रमुवाच ह ।\nउपपद्येत्कथं देव स्त्रियो मम जयो युधि ।\nस्त्रीभावेन च मे गाढं मनः शान्तमुमापते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the maiden again said to Rudra: \"How, O god, can a woman win in battle? And my mind, O husband of Uma, is deeply sunk in my womanhood.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"प्रतिश्रुतश्च भूतेश त्वया भीष्मपराजयः ।\nयथा स सत्यो भवति तथा कुरु वृषध्वज ।\nयथा हन्यां समागम्य भीष्मं शांतनवं युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You have promised, lord of beings, that Bhishma will be defeated. Make that come true, O bearer of the bull banner, so that I may meet and kill Bhishma, son of Shantanu, in battle.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"तामुवाच महादेवः कन्यां किल वृषध्वजः ।\nन मे वागनृतं भद्रे प्राह सत्यं भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Mahadeva, the bull-bannered god, said to the maiden: \"My word is never false, good lady; what I have said will come true.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"वधिष्यसि रणे भीष्मं पुरुषत्वं च लप्स्यसे ।\nस्मरिष्यसि च तत्सर्वं देहमन्यं गता सती ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You will kill Bhishma in battle and you will gain manhood. Having gone into another body, you will remember all this.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"द्रुपदस्य कुले जाता भविष्यसि महारथः ।\nशीघ्रास्त्रश्चित्रयोधी च भविष्यसि सुसंमतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You will be born in Drupada's family and become a great chariot-warrior, quick with weapons, a skilled and esteemed fighter in varied ways.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"यथोक्तमेव कल्याणि सर्वमेतद्भविष्यति ।\nभविष्यसि पुमान्पश्चात्कस्माच्चित्कालपर्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"All this will happen as I have said, lovely one. After some turn of time, you will become a man.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा महातेजाः कपर्दी वृषभध्वजः ।\nपश्यतामेव विप्राणां तत्रैवान्तरधीयत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, the radiant, matted-haired god of the bull banner vanished right there before the eyes of the Brahmins."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततः सा पश्यतां तेषां महर्षीणामनिन्दिता ।\nसमाहृत्य वनात्तस्मात्काष्ठानि वरवर्णिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, as the sages watched, the blameless, fair maiden gathered wood from that forest."}},{"n":17,"text":"चितां कृत्वा सुमहतीं प्रदाय च हुताशनम् ।\nप्रदीप्तेऽग्नौ महाराज रोषदीप्तेन चेतसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"She made a very large pyre and lit the fire; and when the fire blazed, O great king, her mind ablaze with anger,"}},{"n":18,"text":"उक्त्वा भीष्मवधायेति प्रविवेश हुताशनम् ।\nज्येष्ठा काशिसुता राजन्यमुनामभितो नदीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"she said, \"This is for Bhishma's death,\" and entered the fire, that eldest daughter of the king of Kashi, beside the river Yamuna."}}]}]}